---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import NavBar from "../components/NavBar.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="ShipGlows | Product and commercial boundary"
  description="ShipGlows is an autonomous software product, not a service offer. Cockpit SaaS remains a future possibility, not a current offer."
>
  <main class="page-shell">
    <NavBar />

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Product Boundary</p>
        <h1 class="page-title">ShipGlows is software, not a service business.</h1>
        <p>
          The business-partner promise is delivered by the autonomous product:
          governed context, useful judgment, accountable métier workflows, and
          observable proof. It does not hide a consulting or implementation
          offer behind the word “partner”.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="pricing-grid">
        <article class="price-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Available Today</p>
          <h2>The ShipGlows product</h2>
          <p>
            Evaluate and use ShipGlows through its repository, documentation,
            métier skills, governance contracts, and delivery tooling.
          </p>
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>autonomous software behavior</li>
            <li>documentation-led product discovery</li>
            <li>no consulting, diagnostics, or implementation missions</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="price-card accent-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Possible Later</p>
          <h2>A distinct Cockpit SaaS</h2>
          <p>
            Cockpit may eventually become the SaaS product built on this
            direction. It does not exist today and is not being sold or
            presented as available.
          </p>
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>no current availability promise</li>
            <li>no committed roadmap or pricing</li>
            <li>separate product decision required before launch</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Commercial Status</p>
        <h2>There is no service offer and no Cockpit offer today.</h2>
        <p>
          Pricing and monetization remain open until a real product and evidence
          justify them. ShipGlows will not use consulting as an interim business
          model or market an unbuilt SaaS.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="cta-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Start With The Product</p>
        <h2>Inspect what ShipGlows can prove today.</h2>
        <p>
          The repository and documentation show the product behavior, its
          governance model, and the evidence boundary behind the promise.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="/docs">Browse the docs</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="https://github.com/commandglows/shipglows">Open GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
